WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.250


2
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.000
<b>Lord Krishna,</b>

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.958
<b>calling to rise above the definitions of</b>
<b>the living and the dead, says,</b>

4
00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:39.041
<b>"Arjuna,</b>

5
00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:46.625
<b>there was never a time in the past when I, you,</b>
<b>and all these kings did not exist.</b>

6
00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:47.750
<b>In the future too,</b>

7
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.208
<b>there will never be a time when</b>
<b>we all will not be here."</b>

8
00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:57.208


9
00:00:57.208 --> 00:01:01.333
<b>Lord Krishna is speaking here about</b>
<b>the immortality of the soul.</b>

10
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:02.916
<b>Arjuna was worried</b>

11
00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:05.708
<b>that many warriors would be killed in this war,</b>

12
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:10.916
<b>and among them would be his</b>
<b>family members, elders, and relatives.</b>

13
00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:14.583
<b>Here, Lord Krishna is answering</b>
<b>that very concern of Arjuna.</b>

14
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:19.541
<b>He says that the true existence of</b>
<b>a human being is eternal, infinite.</b>

15
00:01:19.541 --> 00:01:22.500
<b>That existence was in the past, is in the present,</b>

16
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.875
<b>and will continue to exist infinitely</b>
<b>into the future.</b>

17
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:28.083
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna had said</b>

18
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:33.250
<b>that a true wise person does not grieve for</b>
<b>either the living or the dead,</b>

19
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.000
<b>and</b>

20
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.041
<b>here he explains why such grief is</b>
<b>meaningless for a learned person.</b>

21
00:01:40.041 --> 00:01:44.833
<b>This is because our true existence is the soul.</b>

22
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:46.541
<b>The soul is imperishable,</b>

23
00:01:46.541 --> 00:01:47.458
<b>immortal,</b>

24
00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:49.750
<b>has been present since time immemorial,</b>

25
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:50.416
<b>and</b>

26
00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:52.083
<b>will continue to exist.</b>

27
00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:52.875
<b>Then what</b>

28
00:01:52.875 --> 00:01:55.041
<b>is there to grieve about?</b>

29
00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:58.083
<b>Here, he also refutes the notion that</b>

30
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:02.500
<b>after attaining liberation,</b>
<b>the soul merges with God.</b>

31
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.666
<b>He is making it absolutely clear through</b>
<b>his words that he himself, Arjuna,</b>

32
00:02:07.666 --> 00:02:10.083
<b>and all the kings around them</b>

33
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:15.125
<b>were present in the past and will continue</b>
<b>to be present in the future.</b>

34
00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:18.916
<b>This means that each soul has its own existence,</b>

35
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:20.791
<b>which always remains;</b>

36
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:23.250
<b>this existence is never lost,</b>

37
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:27.541
<b>whether that soul is currently bound to a body</b>

38
00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:28.333
<b>or</b>

39
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:32.791
<b>attains liberation in the future</b>
<b>and becomes free.</b>

40
00:02:32.791 --> 00:02:37.875
<b>In both these situations,</b>
<b>the soul's own existence is eternal.</b>

41
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:42.666


42
00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:45.791
<b>Ponder for a moment.</b>

43
00:02:45.791 --> 00:02:51.000
<b>What is the root cause of fear</b>
<b>and insecurity in life?</b>

44
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:58.416
<b>Is it not the fear that something dear to you</b>
<b>might be taken away from you?</b>

45
00:02:58.416 --> 00:02:59.833
<b>Your fame,</b>

46
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:01.125
<b>your prosperity,</b>

47
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:02.416
<b>your wealth,</b>

48
00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:03.416
<b>your health.</b>

49
00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:06.750
<b>Or something else.</b>

50
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:13.416
<b>And what is the thought that</b>
<b>frightens you the most?</b>

51
00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:16.333
<b>The answer to this question lies</b>

52
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:19.416
<b>in what is most dear to you.</b>

53
00:03:19.416 --> 00:03:21.208
<b>It's your life,</b>

54
00:03:21.208 --> 00:03:23.125
<b>isn't it?</b>

55
00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:29.958
<b>This is why death is the greatest fear of humans.</b>

56
00:03:29.958 --> 00:03:31.166
<b>But</b>

57
00:03:31.166 --> 00:03:36.375
<b>what if it becomes known that our</b>
<b>existence is actually immortal,</b>

58
00:03:36.375 --> 00:03:38.333
<b>that we are invincible?</b>

59
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:39.916
<b>Then?</b>

60
00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:45.583
<b>Then even the fear of death will</b>
<b>become baseless, won't it?</b>

61
00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:47.000
<b>Something that existed yesterday,</b>

62
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.458
<b>exists in the present,</b>

63
00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:50.916
<b>and will continue to exist in the future</b>

64
00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:56.583
<b>the question of losing such a continuous</b>
<b>existence doesn't even arise.</b>

65
00:03:56.583 --> 00:04:01.958
<b>And what is there to fear about something</b>
<b>that cannot be lost at all?</b>

66
00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:04.666
<b>How liberating is this thought!</b>

67
00:04:04.666 --> 00:04:08.125
<b>It's as if by adopting this single thought,</b>

68
00:04:08.125 --> 00:04:12.666
<b>you gain the strength to break all your bonds.</b>

69
00:04:12.666 --> 00:04:15.916
<b>If a person has understood this eternal truth</b>
<b>and has accepted</b>

70
00:04:15.916 --> 00:04:19.750
<b>it deep within their heart,</b>

71
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.541
<b>no external fear can even touch them.</b>

72
00:04:24.208 --> 00:04:27.833


73
00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:35.666
<b>It is natural for us to love our</b>
<b>family members immensely.</b>

74
00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:37.458
<b>But</b>

75
00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:42.666
<b>one day or another, they will</b>
<b>depart from our midst,</b>

76
00:04:42.666 --> 00:04:44.625
<b>which is also certain.</b>

77
00:04:44.625 --> 00:04:47.416
<b>It is also possible</b>

78
00:04:47.416 --> 00:04:51.833
<b>that we ourselves may leave before them.</b>

79
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:56.250
<b>The thought of such separation from</b>
<b>family becomes very difficult.</b>

80
00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.875
<b>However,</b>

81
00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:00.333
<b>if we come to know</b>

82
00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:05.708
<b>that only their one body has come to an end,</b>

83
00:05:05.708 --> 00:05:10.375
<b>and that they are still alive in the form of a soul.</b>

84
00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:16.500
<b>They have merely left one body</b>
<b>and entered another.</b>

85
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:23.000
<b>Consider it as if they now reside in</b>
<b>another city, another country,</b>

86
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.541
<b>where we can no longer</b>
<b>communicate with them,</b>

87
00:05:26.541 --> 00:05:29.875
<b>but they are well.</b>

88
00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:35.916
<b>This thought can somewhat lessen our anguish.</b>

89
00:05:35.916 --> 00:05:37.208
<b>Because</b>

90
00:05:37.208 --> 00:05:40.250
<b>true love says this, doesn't it,</b>

91
00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.458
<b>that those who are dear</b>

92
00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:44.333
<b>to us should be fine,</b>

93
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.125
<b>wherever they may be.</b>

94
00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:48.625
<b>For all of us, </b>

95
00:05:48.625 --> 00:05:52.500
<b>this body is just a stopover.</b>

96
00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:55.666
<b>The journey of the soul will continue,</b>

97
00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:58.958
<b>the stops will keep changing.</b>

98
00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.958
<b>From this spiritual perspective we can see</b>

99
00:06:01.958 --> 00:06:06.333
<b>that death never really occurs to anyone.</b>

100
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.708


101
00:06:10.708 --> 00:06:12.458
<b>In professional life,</b>

102
00:06:12.458 --> 00:06:16.916
<b> this worry must have often consumed you.</b>

103
00:06:16.916 --> 00:06:20.791
<b>That someone else is doing</b>
<b>better than you at work,</b>

104
00:06:20.791 --> 00:06:23.625
<b>that they might surpass you.</b>

105
00:06:23.625 --> 00:06:24.541
<b>Or</b>

106
00:06:24.541 --> 00:06:31.250
<b>it might happen that someone else takes</b>
<b>your position, your prestige.</b>

107
00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:35.375
<b>If death cannot erase our existence,</b>

108
00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:42.333
<b>then this fear of losing position, the worry of</b>
<b>falling behind in professional competition,</b>

109
00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:45.500
<b>all of this is trivial, isn't it?</b>

110
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.666
<b>Why lament over it?</b>

111
00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:53.833
<b>Our real existence is infinite, indestructible.</b>

112
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:57.500
<b>Then what is the fear of losing something?</b>

113
00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.625
<b>If we adopt this perspective,</b>

114
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:04.000
<b>then our effort will only be</b>

115
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:12.541
<b>to make our best contribution in this one</b>
<b>stopover of our continuous journey, in this life.</b>

116
00:07:12.541 --> 00:07:17.125
<b>And this contribution depends only on us,</b>

117
00:07:17.125 --> 00:07:20.333
<b>not on anyone else.</b>

118
00:07:20.333 --> 00:07:23.416
<b>In this perspective, mental insecurity</b>

119
00:07:23.416 --> 00:07:27.708
<b>and anxiety about the future will all vanish.</b>

120
00:07:27.708 --> 00:07:28.708
<b>Because</b>

121
00:07:28.708 --> 00:07:32.041
<b>no one can destroy us at all.</b>

